From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: File Explorer as the prototype draws it

The approved Windows 11 prototype (PS5_Proton prototypes/windows11-shell) draws File Explorer as Windows 11 does: a
48-pixel title bar of Mica Alt with the tab and the caption buttons, the address row, the command bar, the navigation
pane, Home and the status bar. Wine's browser window with PS5_Proton's earlier decoration (patch 0983) had a classic
caption, a combo box address bar and a row of text buttons. The drawing and the state live in PS5_Proton's
pw_shell_explorer.h (wine/ps5), included here; this patch hands it the window:

- Every message of a Mihawk Explorer window goes to pw_explorer_message first; the earlier per-message decoration is
  gone. The window's state is one pointer (explorer_info.ui).
- Without a folder on the command line Explorer starts on Home, as Windows 11's does, and browses nothing until asked.
- The window's title is the location's name and " - File Explorer" (pw_explorer_title), not the bare name.
- Ctrl+L, Alt+D, Alt+arrows and F5 go to the window wherever the focus is (pw_explorer_key).
- update_path_box does nothing without a path box (the Mihawk window has none).
- The browser control has no border (EBO_NOBORDER, set before IExplorerBrowser_Initialize, which decides it): the
  prototype's items sit straight on the window.
---
